      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To initiate the computer repair process, begin by examining the hardware."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening unit implicitly starts the process and describes the initial examination step. The model splits this into an explicit start node and two equivalent actions, preserving behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "label:n2->n3",
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the hardware has been checked, proceed with repairing any issues that were identified."
      ],
      "justification": "The label captures the conditional context ('Issues found') and the action models the repair step. Re-typing a condition as a label does not change behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "label:n3->n4",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After the necessary repairs have been made, conclude the hardware inspection."
      ],
      "justification": "The label and action faithfully restate the completion and conclusion steps described in the source."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Following the completion of the repair process, it is important to test the functionality of the system."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of the testing step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the test results indicate that everything is functioning properly, then the hardware inspection process can be concluded."
      ],
      "justification": "The branch opens the decision, the guard abstracts the positive condition using a variable but preserves the logic, and the action/end capture the conclusion path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n7",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the test results indicate that there are still issues, then further hardware repairs are required."
      ],
      "justification": "The guard correctly captures the negative condition ('Issues remain') and the action models the required further repairs."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "label:n7->n8",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once these additional repairs have been made, the hardware inspection process can be concluded."
      ],
      "justification": "The label, action, and end node accurately reflect the final repair completion and process conclusion described in the text."
    }
  ],
